                            <comment id="14607948" author="felixcheung" created="Tue, 30 Jun 2015 08:34:34 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This is likely because the editor mode is never changed.&lt;br/&gt;
From before, &lt;br/&gt;
1. (start typing in cell) editor mode: scala&lt;br/&gt;
2. (type %sql) editor mode: scala  - does not apply as expected&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Whereas when loading a previous notebook for the expected editor mode is applied when the notebook is loaded, resulting in slightly different syntax highlighting in these two cases.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14653967" author="tzolov" created="Tue, 4 Aug 2015 16:56:47 +0000"  >
&lt;p&gt;The auto-completion is initialized in the paragraph.controller.js aceLoaded. Currently it looks like this:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;$scope.aceLoaded = function(_editor) {
....
  $scope.editor.setOptions(
      {enableBasicAutocompletion: &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;,enableSnippets: &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;, enableLiveAutocompletion:&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;});

   &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; remoteCompleter = {getCompletions : function(editor, session, pos, prefix, callback) {...}};
   
   langTools.addCompleter(remoteCompleter);
}
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We can use &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;langTools.setCompleters([remoteCompleter]);&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt; instead (e.g. not ADD but SET) to restrict the completion suggestions to those provided by the interpreters.  Also we should move the  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;enableBasicAutocompletion: &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;true&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt; setting after the &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;langTools.setCompletters(..) &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt; as suggested here: &lt;a href=&quot;http://stackoverflow.com/questions/26991288/ace-editor-autocompletion-remove-local-variables&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://stackoverflow.com/questions/26991288/ace-editor-autocompletion-remove-local-variables&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The end configuration sequence would look like this:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;$scope.aceLoaded = function(_editor) {
....
   &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; remoteCompleter = {getCompletions : function(editor, session, pos, prefix, callback) {...}};
   
   langTools.setCompleters([remoteCompleter]);

  $scope.editor.setOptions(
      {enableBasicAutocompletion: &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;,enableSnippets: &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;, enableLiveAutocompletion:&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;});
}
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Although this seem to resolve this issue i wonder if there is something else we should consider? &lt;/p&gt;
</comment>
